WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.240
A blurry photograph of a man in a black cowl
is taped to the wall.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.040
A black knife held by a tattooed hand pierces
his face.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.900
“You want him dead?”

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.900
Able asked.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.000
“Dealt with,” his Foundation handler replied.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.430
“Same thing…”

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.010
Able said, and laughed.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.160
The helicopter was ready to go outside.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.230
It was another rainy night, almost all of
them were.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:29.300
Plumes of black smoke billowing from factories
on the far side of the city, blotting out

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.900
the already darkened sky and plunging Gotham
into deeper shadow.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:40.590
But those shadows, that darkness, were something
the twisted underbelly had come to fear.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:46.980
The dark was a tool that one man used to prey
on those who enacted injustice on the innocent.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:52.449
Every shadowy alley, or flutter of movement
atop a roof, made every thief and murder on

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:57.000
the streets of Gotham take pause, think twice.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.820
Batman had been trailing the movements of
suspicious cargo trucks moving in and out

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:02.070
of the city.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:06.479
Some were decoys, driving around with empty
containers and changing their routes every

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:10.659
night to throw the World’s Greatest Detective
off the trail.

00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:15.750
But those were just a distraction, a theatrical
deception being deployed so that the real

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.630
cargo could be smuggled in undetected.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:24.750
Bane, a muscle-bound mercenary with the guise
of a luchador, was one of Batman’s most

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.130
physically imposing enemies.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:31.730
For weeks, he had been stockpiling Venom,
a strength-enhancing compound, somewhere in

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:32.799
the city.

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:37.799
And now, Batman had picked up the trail; the
trucks weren’t distributing the Venom, that

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:43.600
was being done by a network of low-level street
thugs posing as motorcycle delivery drivers.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.890
Swooping through the night sky, watching one
of the bikers from above, there was something

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:49.850
else playing on the Dark Knight’s mind.

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:53.240
Recently, he’d gotten the feeling he was
being watched.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.820
At first, the man under the cowl – billionaire
philanthropist Bruce Wayne – had chalked

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:03.460
it up to paranoia, a side effect of his nightly
escapades as the Caped Crusader.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:07.920
His trusted butler and confidant Alfred had
even suggested as much.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.450
But as the weeks rolled on, Batman couldn’t
shrug the notion that every move he made,

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:18.140
every case he helped Commissioner Gordon solve,
every battle with the worst of Gotham’s

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:21.819
rogue’s gallery, that somebody was studying
him.

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:26.890
Already, Bruce had a list of potential suspects,
the likely candidates for who were having

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:27.959
him followed.

00:02:27.959 --> 00:02:32.630
So, he gradually began paying them all visits
as his alter ego.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:37.239
The larger of the city’s mob families, the
Falcones, denied any involvement.

00:02:37.239 --> 00:02:41.989
With their leader Carmine Falcone currently
behind bars, the rest of the family were laying

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:45.349
low to avoid being arrested themselves.

00:02:45.349 --> 00:02:51.370
Next came Hugo Strange, a brilliant but unhinged
scientist whom had been obsessed with Batman

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.069
for a number of years.

00:02:53.069 --> 00:02:57.310
Bruce had worried that Hugo had finally cracked
the secret of his true identity.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:01.980
But the despicable doctor also refuted that
he was the one having the Dark Knight followed.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:06.989
The next possible culprit on the list was
Amanda Waller, a powerful and high-ranking

00:03:06.989 --> 00:03:12.210
government operative, strategic genius, and
another of Batman’s rivals.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:17.160
Known to some as The Wall, she was responsible
for a number of shady, covert operations that

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.909
not even the Caped Crusader knew about.

00:03:19.909 --> 00:03:25.209
Waller dealt in secrets, and seemed just as
likely to be having Batman tailed in order

00:03:25.209 --> 00:03:27.060
to pick up dirt on the detective.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:33.040
But, as with Strange and the Falcones, Amanda
Waller denied all of the Dark Knight’s claims;

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.049
the heartbeat scanners built into his cowl’s
eyepieces confirmed that they had all been

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.959
telling the truth.

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:43.040
Shrugging the notion off, Batman focused on
following the biker transporting Venom across

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.120
the city, silently gliding between skyscrapers
with his cape.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.890
He followed the smuggler all the way to an
abandoned chemical processing plant, formerly

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:54.970
owned by a company called ACE Chemical.

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:59.849
He suspected that was where Bane and his thugs
had established a base of operations, using

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:04.550
the plant’s leftover equipment to refine
the Venom, the source of Bane’s inhuman

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.550
strength.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:09.790
Scanning through the rooftop with his cowl’s
x-ray capabilities, from a distance Batman

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:13.030
spotted a group of armed men unloading boxes.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:16.859
They were acting under the command of a larger
figure: Bane himself.

00:04:16.859 --> 00:04:23.100
But then, it appeared a new, unidentified
figure had come striding into the building,

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.150
met with hostility as Bane’s forces drew
their weapons.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:29.030
Whoever this was, he clearly wasn’t with
them.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:33.389
Suddenly, just as Batman fired his grappling
hook to swing onto the roof of the chemical

00:04:33.389 --> 00:04:36.230
plant, all-out chaos erupted inside.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:41.780
Down below, watched intently by Batman as
he slipped inside, staying concealed in the

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:46.460
rafters, the new figure had begun violently
attacking Bane and his men.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:51.560
The man was lean, shirtless, around his late
twenties, with grey eyes and a mess of jet

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.770
black hair.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:59.520
His entire body was covered in tattoos depicting
arcane runes and occult imagery on his olive

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.520
skin.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:05.020
In his hands had appeared a pair of sharp,
black blades, seemingly from nowhere.

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:10.020
To some, he was Hevel ben Adam, the Butcher
of the West, the Great Traitor and First Sword

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.020
of Daevon.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:17.319
But to the ones that had sent him there, he
was SCP-076-2: Able.

00:05:17.319 --> 00:05:21.250
He charged towards the group of thugs as they
opened fire, their bullets missing as Able

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.290
moved with incredible speed.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:27.650
With a strong upward swing of both his swords,
he cleaved the nearest two mercenaries’

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:33.150
weapons into broken pieces, as if their guns
were made of plastic, not metal.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:38.270
Able brought both swords slicking downwards,
felling both men simultaneously.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:42.600
Another nearby turned and ran, only to be
caught by one of Able’s blades as the barbaric

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.240
warrior hurled it through the air.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.479
Watching from above, Batman was taken aback.

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:52.290
It was rare for him to be so alarmed by a
display of violence, especially given he had

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.780
devoted his life to crime fighting.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:06:00.340
But the figure below was taking on Bane’s
men singlehandedly, with such speed and aggression,

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.740
that it gave the Caped Crusader pause.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:07.930
As much as he abhorred killing, Batman held
back to observe this new adversary, as Able

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:10.710
squared up against Bane himself.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:15.680
The luchador charged at him with the unbridled
rage of a snarling, feral animal, while Able

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.490
leaped into battle with equal ferocity.

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:23.590
His hand reached into a tiny dimensional rift,
a hole in space out of which he retrieved

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:26.949
an extra weapon that he swung directly at
Bane’s head.

00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:31.440
The imposing muscle monster caught the blade
in his huge hand, blocking the blow.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:36.050
He lifted Able off the ground, his own hand
still gripping the sword by its hilt, and

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:40.150
was about to deliver a crippling punch that
would have sent the barbarian flying.

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:45.290
That is, had he not slipped another sword
seemingly out of thin air and used it to slice

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.360
through the blade that Bane had in his grip.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.760
Batman had only ever seen combatants with
Able’s level of fighting prowess among the

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:57.849
ranks of the Court of Owls and League of Assassins,
ancient orders of killers who operated in

00:06:57.849 --> 00:06:58.849
secret.

00:06:58.849 --> 00:07:03.039
Maybe this barbaric fighter was part of such
an organization, maybe Able had been watching

00:07:03.039 --> 00:07:04.039
him?

00:07:04.039 --> 00:07:09.090
The Detective watched and pondered over possible
connections to Ra’s Al Ghul, Talon and even

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.380
Azrael as Able took on the mountainous mercenary.

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:17.110
He had ducked out of the way of an oncoming
swipe, rolling between the wrestler’s legs

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:18.870
in an open stance.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:23.940
Having outflanked Bane, before he had a chance
to turn around and face him, Able jumped upwards,

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:27.410
a pair of his black, reflective swords in
hand.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:31.530
Slashing both through the air, he severed
the tubes on Bane’s back, part of a harness

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:36.250
designed to pump the Venom chemical into his
body and enhance his strength.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:41.199
Sickly green fluid spewed from the pipes,
with Bane reaching his muscular arms behind

00:07:41.199 --> 00:07:45.100
him, fumbling with the mechanism, desperately
trying to repair the device that kept his

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.139
body strong.

00:07:46.139 --> 00:07:51.490
It was too late, the luchador dropped to his
knees and collapsed, defeated as Able stood

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.650
over him with his swords in hand.

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:56.919
“You can come out now, Bat!” he called
up to the ceiling.

00:07:56.919 --> 00:08:00.810
“By now, you have no doubt guessed that
I’m not here for this one.

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:03.880
It’s you they sent me to find.”

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:08.610
Never one to charge headfirst into a fight
without thought, Batman dropped a smoke pellet.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:13.580
It burst as it made contact with the concrete
floor below, filling the area around Able

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:18.020
with a heavy, grey fog that was impossible
for the warrior to see through.

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:22.479
A trio of sharp-tipped Batarangs came spinning
through the air; Able barely had a chance

00:08:22.479 --> 00:08:26.949
to see them coming in time to block them with
his swords, only to be caught off guard as

00:08:26.949 --> 00:08:29.380
an attack struck him from behind.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:34.630
Dropping from above, Batman landed a devastating
gliding kick, knocking Able to the ground.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:39.410
The barbarian rolled over, angered at the
outmaneuver, as Batman stood casting a towering,

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:41.550
pointy-eared shadow over him.

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:43.229
“Who are you?”

00:08:43.229 --> 00:08:47.900
Batman demanded in the deep, authoritative
voice of a grizzled veteran vigilante.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:54.149
“I am known by many names,” the man replied,
the Detective taking note of his distinctive

00:08:54.149 --> 00:08:55.350
Middle Eastern accent.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:59.500
“You will call me Able, the man who will
be your undoing.”

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:04.890
“Tell me who sent you,” the Dark Knight
retorted, adding, “Or else.”

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:08.600
Able chuckled dryly before swinging one of
his swords downwards.

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:12.620
Blocking it with his gauntlets, Batman trapped
the blade between the row of claws on his

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:16.360
forearms, before using them to snap the weapon
in two.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:20.100
Just as Able went to stab at him with his
other one, the Dark Knight spun out of the

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:25.140
way, grabbing his opponent’s hand and guiding
the weapon away in a smooth parry, telling

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:27.180
of his years of martial arts training.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:32.020
But, with both hands holding Able’s attack
aloft, Batman couldn’t prevent the barbarian

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:35.279
from pulling yet another blade from his pocket
dimension.

00:09:35.279 --> 00:09:40.010
With a slash from a smaller knife, Able cleaved
open the grey and black costumed that the

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:43.390
Caped Crusader wore, causing him a serious
injury.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:48.800
Grunting in pain, Batman headbutted Able square
in the nose, causing him to reel back, still

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.700
chuckling at the tenacity of his target.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.390
“Impressive,” Able mused.

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:55.790
“The Foundation sent me here to kill you.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:59.350
I wasn’t expecting to find such a worthy
adversary.”

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:04.080
He slowly lowered his swords, while Batman
kept his fists raised in a fighting stance.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.210
“I will not be their puppet.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:09.860
You and I are both warriors,” the barbarian
stated.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.920
“I’m not a killer,” Batman argued.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:17.860
“Perhaps, but you are a fighter, and a fighting
man does not deserve to be killed like a sheep,

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:23.709
at the behest of cowards and fools… you
deserve a warrior’s death,” Able replied.

00:10:23.709 --> 00:10:26.370
“Two hours from now, midnight.

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:29.730
We meet atop the tallest building in this
wretched city.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:33.450
There and then, that is when you die at my
hand.”

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.840
With that, Able turned and walked away.

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:39.730
Batman thought about going after him, tackling
him to the ground and restraining him.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:43.060
But he was still wounded, he needed time to
recuperate.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:44.540
“I checked the records, sir.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:48.779
There is no mention of any metahuman with
the power to create weapons on either the

00:10:48.779 --> 00:10:54.070
ARGUS or STAR Labs databases,” Alfred explained
over Batman’s earpiece.

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:57.990
After a quick retreat to the cave to tend
to his injury, Bruce was already racing back

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.930
out into the night, careening through the
streets of Gotham in the Batmobile.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:05.460
“What about the ‘Foundation’ that Able
mentioned?” he asked Alfred.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:09.350
“Not much luck there either, Master Bruce,”
his faithful butler answered.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:14.060
“There is one mention of an organization
called the ‘SCP Foundation’ in an old

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:17.600
ARGUS document, but the majority of the file
has been redacted.

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:21.720
The only reference to it is in an addendum
that someone must have forgotten to remove.”

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:24.240
“Good work, Alfred,” Batman responded.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:27.940
“There’s one person in this city who might
be able to give me more information.”

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:30.399
“Oh, heavens, you don’t mean…”

00:11:30.399 --> 00:11:32.880
“Who else has a knack for knowing too much?”

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:38.060
The cell was quiet, lit only by the low flickering
of fluorescent bulbs that hung from the ceiling

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.339
of Arkham Asylum.

00:11:39.339 --> 00:11:43.960
It had been hours since the guards had called
for the inmates to go to bed, although they

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.829
were no less alert.

00:11:45.829 --> 00:11:48.290
Any one of them could break out at any time.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:51.550
And there was one who’d been waiting for
his chance rather patiently.

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:56.740
“Riddle me this,” Edward said aloud, aware
of a figure approaching his cell.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:58.760
“I am always around but unseen.

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:01.220
I am often avoided but never outrun.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:05.180
I could find you at the end of the road or
even the next corner.

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:06.970
What am I?”

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:09.089
“Death,” Batman answered monotonously.

00:12:09.089 --> 00:12:12.550
“To what do I owe the pleasure, Dark Knight?”

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:13.550
the Riddler asked.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:16.250
“I need information,” the Caped Crusader
replied.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.449
“And you’ve got more than your fair share.”

00:12:18.449 --> 00:12:23.660
“After a decade of rivalry, the Detective
decides to come crawling to me for answers,

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:27.050
to offer some recognition of my brilliance!”

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:28.820
“Not brilliance, Edward.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.040
Persistence,” he corrected.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:33.250
“Hm, you’re as cheery as ever,” the
Riddler chuckled.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.120
“The SCP Foundation, what do you know?”

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:39.320
He peered over the rim of his glasses, offering
Batman a wry smile.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.480
“If you know me, you’ll want to share
me.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.910
If you share me, I’ll be gone.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:46.690
What am I?” he asked.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:47.690
“A secret.”

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.990
“Oh, they certainly are!”

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.490
Edward exploded with laughter.

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:53.870
“The Foundation are an odd bunch.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:59.660
They’d even make some of the patients here
at good old Arkham seem sane by comparison.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:04.950
Think of them as the resident experts in unusual
phenomena, ‘anomalies’ they call them,”

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.079
the maniac obsessed with mind games explained.

00:13:07.079 --> 00:13:13.250
“They are everywhere, all across the world,
an organization older and with more reach

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:14.720
than any you’ve encountered.

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:20.149
And oh me, oh my, the things that they have
locked away... monsters that would scare even

00:13:20.149 --> 00:13:21.149
you, Batman.”

00:13:21.149 --> 00:13:24.140
“How do I know this isn’t another one
of your delusions, Riddler?”

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:27.970
Batman barked, banging a fist against the
bars to intimidate his nemesis.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:30.470
“Don’t insult me, Dark Knight!

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:34.830
You and I both know you wouldn’t have come
to me if you were going to disbelieve what

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.730
I had to say,” the Riddler yelled.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:41.070
“And mark my words, if the Foundation has
its sights on you, well…

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:45.180
Riddle me this –”
Already Batman had turned and started walking

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:46.889
away down the corridor.

00:13:46.889 --> 00:13:52.130
“My inventor doesn’t want me, the man
who bought me won’t need me, and the man

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.639
who needs me doesn’t know it.

00:13:54.639 --> 00:13:56.570
What am I?”

00:13:56.570 --> 00:13:58.800
The Dark Knight paused a few feet from the
cell.

00:13:58.800 --> 00:13:59.800
“A coffin.”

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:04.070
“It could all be a trick, sir,” Alfred
urged as Bruce departed the Asylum.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:07.399
“Edward Nashton is hardly a reliable source
of information.”

00:14:07.399 --> 00:14:12.209
“He has a compulsion to always prove himself
as the smartest, to always be right,” Batman

00:14:12.209 --> 00:14:16.000
replied, “What I still can’t understand
is why this Foundation would send Able to

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.000
kill me?

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.290
What’s the connection between them and me?”

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:23.680
“Perhaps, Master Bruce, it’s less what
connects you and more how you could be an

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:26.079
obstacle to them,” the butler reasoned.

00:14:26.079 --> 00:14:31.430
“If this Foundation are experts in unusual
phenomena, then there are an abundance of

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.600
such things here in Gotham.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.750
Everything from the copious super criminals
to the giant coin here in the Batcave.”

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:41.680
“And with me out of the way,” Batman began
to catch on.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:45.010
“They’d have free reign,” Alfred finished
the sentence.

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:50.330
“In sending a madman to kill you, it’s
clear they didn't come to play fair, sir.”

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:54.310
The clocktower in the middle of Gotham let
out an ominous ‘bong’, marking the approach

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:55.310
of midnight.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:58.449
“Then neither will I,” Batman replied.

00:14:58.449 --> 00:15:03.760
Able had been waiting atop the roof of a skyscraper,
the name ‘Wayne Enterprises’ emblazoned

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:04.760
on its front.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:09.410
It was almost midnight, there were minutes
left, but the barbarian was still confident

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:10.740
the Bat would show.

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:16.769
He could almost taste the adrenaline of their
looming battle, anticipating their final showdown.

00:15:16.769 --> 00:15:20.490
Able could hardly wait to have a worthy opponent
to best in combat.

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:24.630
The sound of some kind of advanced aircraft
whooshed overhead, and the barbaric warrior

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:26.579
craned his neck upwards.

00:15:26.579 --> 00:15:31.130
Soaring above was the Batplane, set against
the backdrop of the night sky with a single

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:36.410
beam of light reaching up into the clouds,
projecting the Dark Knight’s insignia above:

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:37.500
the Bat Signal.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:41.720
Parachuting down, Batman had donned a heavily
armored battle suit over his costume.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:45.810
He’d originally designed it to go toe to
toe with Superman in case his closest ally

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:50.370
ever went rogue, but the armor’s bulkier
plating would easily be more resistant to

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:52.829
the ferocious damage Able could dish out.

00:15:52.829 --> 00:15:56.230
He landed on the rooftop with a thud, as Able
jeered in disgust.

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:57.940
“Coward!” he spat.

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:01.889
“You are not the honorable fighter I mistook
you for.

00:16:01.889 --> 00:16:06.690
Just another pretender like that luchador,
giving yourself an advantage rather than rely

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:08.060
on your skill!

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:11.250
Are you so afraid of me that you’d encase
yourself in armor?”

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:13.800
“Are you afraid that you’ll lose?”

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.070
Batman replied calmly.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:19.690
Roaring in anger, Able charged towards Batman,
pulling a fresh pair of swords from his pocket

00:16:19.690 --> 00:16:20.690
dimension.

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:24.580
He swung the blades through the air, only
for them to clang off the thick plating protecting

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:29.620
the Caped Crusader’s arms as he lifted his
gauntlets to block the incoming attacks.

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:35.019
Immediately, feral, bloodthirsty rage on his
face, Able swiped again, this time directing

00:16:35.019 --> 00:16:40.320
his weapon to a tiny gap where Batman’s
helmet met the rest of his suit at the neck.

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:44.550
The sword stayed lodged between the armor,
only for Batman to pull back and launch a

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:47.640
devastating punch that sent Able staggering
back.

00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:50.819
“I built this suit to survive hits from
a Kryptonian.

00:16:50.819 --> 00:16:53.930
Trust me, you won’t even scratch it,”
Batman declared.

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:56.510
“Give it up, Able, walk away.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:58.630
Tell the Foundation to stay out of Gotham.”

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:03.639
Seeing red, noticing one of his weapons was
still stuck at the join in Batman’s armor,

00:17:03.639 --> 00:17:06.900
Able let out a mighty yell and ran towards
his adversary.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:11.020
Stomping forward to clash with him head-on,
Batman started moving as fast as the bulky

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:12.630
Batsuit would allow him.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:17.860
But, moments before the pair of them collided,
Able dropped, skidding along the rooftop under

00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:22.390
Batman’s legs, using the size and weight
of his opponent’s armor to his advantage;

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:25.150
just like he had done with Bane earlier.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:29.350
Before Batman had a chance to turn around,
Able leaped onto his feet and grabbed his

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:33.780
cape, pulling the Dark Knight over and causing
his heavy armor to topple.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:38.250
Batman clattered down onto his back, and Able
gripped the sword that had gotten stuck.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:43.190
With one hand gripping the Bat by his cape,
the barbarian used the other to grab his weapon,

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:46.370
trying to lever off his opponent’s protective
helmet.

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:50.910
Struggling to get himself free, Batman reached
for his belt, throwing a barrage of batarangs

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:55.299
that spun through the air, only to return
and strike Able in the chest.

00:17:55.299 --> 00:17:59.280
He barely registered the impact, shrugging
off the projectiles as if they were made of

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:00.280
paper.

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:01.280
“You cannot win!

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:06.060
Even if you could best me, I always come back,”
Able grunted, feeling his sword breaking through

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.730
the join in Batman’s armor.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:10.260
“I am Able, I am immortal!

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:13.890
But underneath all your tools and tricks,
you are nothing but a man.

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:17.750
Now do what men do and die.”

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:21.230
A sudden, winding blow stuck Able square in
the chest.

00:18:21.230 --> 00:18:25.240
Batman had activated the heartbeat sensors
in his helmet’s eyepieces, and sent both

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:30.200
his armor-plated fists rocketing upwards,
connecting with the barbarian’s heart.

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:35.530
Reeling, Able staggered back, trying to catch
his breath, as Batman stood to his feet, the

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:39.250
hulking, unmistakable silhouette towering
over the immortal warrior.

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:42.380
“I’m not just a man,” he growled.

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:44.390
“I am vengeance!”

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:45.390
Bam!

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.860
His words were punctuated by another devastating
punch to the same spot.

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.470
“I am the night!”

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:51.470
Pow!

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:54.860
Once more, the Dark Knight struck Able in
the heart, sending him closer to the edge

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:55.940
of the roof.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:57.809
“I am Batman!”

00:18:57.809 --> 00:19:02.890
A thundercrack rang out, as Able looked up
wheezing at his adversary.

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:03.890
“You…

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:06.640
you will not kill me, Bat,” he rasped.

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:09.539
“No, I won’t,” Batman answered, leaning
in close.

00:19:09.539 --> 00:19:11.460
“You always come back.”

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:16.049
With a final uppercut, he knocked Able over
the ledge, sending the barbarian careening

00:19:16.049 --> 00:19:18.900
down into the Gotham Reservoir below.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:23.040
Despite being exhausted from their encounter,
Batman scoured the reservoir for any signs

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:24.260
of Able’s remains.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:29.450
He couldn’t find anything, there was no
body, but something told the Dark Knight that

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:32.179
the undying barbarian would be back.

00:19:32.179 --> 00:19:36.030
From a distant rooftop, a pair of Foundation
operatives were watching through night vision

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:37.030
scopes.

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:39.900
“Well, that seemed a little excessive,”
one remarked to the other.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:41.900
“Didn’t think he was the type to show-off.”

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:45.330
“I don’t think that was showing off,”
the other replied.

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:47.520
“I think that was a warning.”

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:53.800
Now go and check out “DEADPOOL VS SCP-682
THE HARD TO DESTROY REPTILE” and “SCP-073

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:58.860
&amp; 076 CAIN VS ABLE”! for more badass battles
from SCP Explained!

